\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces A2.3, the retracted switching result. With circuits correctly bounded by $|G|=2$, a per-circuit price is flat for every $k\ge 2$ and never produces an interior optimum; the previously reported $k=2$ optimum came from charging eight circuits. An interior optimum appears only under a per-switch price on an interleaved schedule.}}{5}{table.6}\protected@file@percent }
